### Page 1 of 2

```text
Amendments made at the June 10, 2020 Committee of the Whole
meeting:
ORDINANCE – 3rd READING – Appropriating moneys for the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming for various
purposes in conducting the municipal government of said City and fixing the amount of general
and special taxes as part of the revenue required to meet the said appropriation, all for the Fiscal
Year beginning July 1, 2020 and ending June 30, 2021.
Amended by adding footnotes #1 through #13 (as listed below) and by adding that the City Treasurer is
given authority as part of this amendment to make any technical amendments to these footnotes and the
budget ordinance to reflect the intent of these footnotes.
-Footnote 1: Authorized General Fund full time positions for FY2021 shall not exceed 382.
-Footnote 2: Salaries of the 382 authorized General Fund positions as well as salaries all other funds shall
not be increased in FY2021 through any type of raise, merit pay, cost of living adjustment, or any other
reason. This footnote excludes members of the Police Department and Fire Union who are governed by
separate compensation agreements.
-Footnote 3: The first $17,500 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as indicated in
Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated to Safe
Harbor.
-Footnote 4: Dollars $17,501-$32,000 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated
to Animal Shelter.
-Footnote 5: Dollars $32,001-$57,000 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 r shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be
appropriated to Laramie County Senior Services.
-Footnote 6: Dollars $57,001-$115,500 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated
to Animal Control.
-Footnote 7: Dollars $115,500-$160,415 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Fire Department budget.
-Footnote 8: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)(iii) “economic development projects”-the first $51,328.26 of federal CARES Act
dollars the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-19 related
expenditures pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the Downtown Development Authority for the
following expenditures:  Emergency Microgrants - $51,328.26.
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
-Footnote 9: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Sections 1(b)(i)&(iv)-the $51,328.27th cent and dollar through the $196,681.27th cent and dollar
of federal CARES Act funds the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-
19 related expenditures pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the City/County Health Department
for expenditures consistent with federal law and SEA 1. If this dollar amount exceeds the eligible
expenditures of the City/County Health Department, the remaining next dollar on will then be prioritized
to the intent of Footnote 10.
-Footnote 10: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)-the $196,681.28th cent and dollar through the $311,681.27th cent and dollar of
federal CARES Act funds the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-
19 related expenditures pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the Alcohol Receiving Center for
expenditures consistent with federal law and SEA 1. If this dollar amount exceeds the eligible expenditures
of the Alcohol Receiving Center, the remaining next dollar on will then be prioritized to the intent of
Footnote 11.
-Footnote 11:  Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)(iv), any CARES Act dollars received by the City of Cheyenne after reimbursement to
the City for direct COVID-19 related expenditures through SEA 1 or otherwise, not spent as set forth in
footnotes 10, 11, 12 shall next be appropriated to eligible expenditures budgeted to be funded by reserves
in FY2021. Said expenditures are related to the $775,000 designated for the Civic Center and the $260,000
Minimum Revenue Guarantee for the Airport.
-Footnote 12:  There are General Fund line items historically rolled over each fiscal year that will not be
rolled over, either in part or in total in FY2021, and will instead be used to fund $17,500 for Safe Harbor,
$15,000 for the Cheyenne Animal Shelter for shelter services, $25,000 for Laramie County Senior Services
and $58,500 for the Cheyenne Animal Shelter for animal control services.  An additional $57,688 will be
used to fund the Fire Department. These rollover line items total $132,685 and include $50,000 in Belvoir
Ranch Planning/Development (001-21-2113-40-43906); $13,216 in Right of Way Purchases/Professional
Fees (001-21-2113-40-43908); $56,196 in Municipal Building Major Replacements (001-21-2113-40-
86935) and $13,273 in Capital Improvement Expenses (001-21-2113-40-32107).  The remaining funds in
the amount of $41,003 will be transferred from the Miscellaneous Department insurance line item as a
result of a lower property, liability and crime coverage rate increase than what was projected.
-Footnote 13:  Move $61,997 from the Miscellaneous Department insurance line item to the Community
Recreation and Events Aquatics Division as a result of a lower property, liability and crime coverage
insurance rate increase than was projected.
The City Treasurer is given authority as part of this amendment to make any technical amendments to
these footnotes and the budget ordinance to reflect the intent of these footnotes.
*Footnote 2 was amended to read: “This footnote excludes seasonal workers and does not prohibit an
employee from being promoted into a pre-existing higher position with a pre-existing higher pay”
```
